---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals consult without doing the implementation?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Consulting can be provided independently where the requirement is assessment, planning, technical guidance or review rather than implementation.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you review a technology proposal from another vendor?",
    answer:
      "Yes. We can review requirements, proposed architecture, scope, technical assumptions and implementation considerations where appropriate.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can consultancy help us decide whether to build custom software?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Build-versus-buy decisions should consider requirements, budget, ownership, flexibility, implementation time, support and long-term operating cost.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you consult on existing systems as well as new projects?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Existing environments can be reviewed for architecture, maintainability, integration, operational problems or improvement opportunities.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you help define project requirements before development starts?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Clarifying objectives, users, workflows, integrations, constraints and acceptance expectations before development can reduce expensive changes later.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Is IT consultancy only for large companies?",
    answer:
      "No. Small and growing businesses can benefit significantly from making better technology decisions before committing limited budgets to unsuitable systems.",
  },
];
---

<section class="consultancy-faq">
  <div class="site-container consultancy-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>IT consultancy FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before committing to the technology decision.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="consultancy-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .consultancy-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .consultancy-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .consultancy-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .consultancy-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .consultancy-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .consultancy-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .consultancy-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .consultancy-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .consultancy-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
